  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>The string of this bow hums before a storm, hours before the first cloud. Archers who have drawn it say the air smells scorched afterward, and that birds stay out of the sky above it for a day.</p><p>You have a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.</p><p>Attacks with this bow have no Disadvantage at long range and ignore Half Cover and Three-Quarters Cover.</p><p><strong>Bolt From the Blue.</strong> Once per day, as an action, you loose an arrow that becomes lightning in a Line 300 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in it makes a [[/save ability=dex dc=20 format=long]], taking [[/damage 12d6 type=lightning]] damage on a failed save or half as much on a success. The bow regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>Weather Answers.</strong> An arrow shot straight up from this bow changes the sky. Within the hour the weather for a mile around becomes what the archer asked for aloud, and stays so until the next dawn. The sky does not take the same request twice in one season.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
